\title{spatialDWLS: cell type deconvolution of spatial spots}
\description{
Estimate what fraction of each spot is made up of each cell type, given a
mean-expression reference built from single-cell data.
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=dwls]{dwls()}} deconvolves an in-memory expression matrix.
\item \code{\link[=dwls_stream]{dwls_stream()}} does the same for a backend that reads spots in windows,
so the expression never has to fit in memory at once.
\item \code{\link[=dwls_signature]{dwls_signature()}} builds the reference from a single-cell matrix.
}
